# Managed by Ansible (roles/hardening) - do not edit by hand.
#
# Every connection to this host, root included, already authenticates by
# key (verified before this was written: root has exactly one
# authorized_keys entry and no other account has usable credentials), so
# turning password auth off changes nothing about how anyone actually logs
# in - it only removes online password guessing as an avenue. fail2ban
# (roles/fail2ban) slows that down; this closes it.

PasswordAuthentication no
PermitRootLogin prohibit-password
X11Forwarding no
ClientAliveInterval 300
ClientAliveCountMax 2
